\title{foresightr: Forecasts Chosen by What Would Have Worked}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.svg}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Time series forecasting that replays the past before trusting a model: a rolling-origin backtest refits every candidate at each origin, the choice is made by out-of-sample error, and prediction intervals are quantiles of the errors actually observed, for each horizon and for totals of the next periods. Models include seasonal 'ARIMA' by exact maximum likelihood with automatic orders, exponential smoothing in state space form, a 'Prophet'-style trend with changepoints and events, 'TBATS', 'STL' and 'MSTL' decompositions, Croston's method and ensembles. The computations are done by the 'Rust' crate 'foresight'.
}
